# Planned special arcs L16-18: data/lore only; not active current UI
growing_villages.special.roots_of_the_road.title=Roots of the Road
growing_villages.special.roots_of_the_road.summary=The memory of the first paths can become a shared grove when the village tends it with care.
growing_villages.special.roots_of_the_road.step_01.objective=Gather records, oak saplings, and light for a future garden of memory.
growing_villages.special.roots_of_the_road.step_01.success=The first names and young trees give the road a human voice again.
growing_villages.special.roots_of_the_road.step_02.objective=Prepare stone, signs, and timber for a quiet place of remembrance.
growing_villages.special.roots_of_the_road.step_02.success=Memory has gained a shore where it can be read and carried onward.
growing_villages.special.roots_of_the_road.step_03.objective=Confirm the shared memorial contribution with books and evening light.
growing_villages.special.roots_of_the_road.step_03.success=The road no longer rests on one name; the whole village keeps it.
growing_villages.special.roots_of_the_road.completion=The memory arc is complete; a future grove will be the visible sign of shared care.
growing_villages.special.roots_of_the_road.build=Future one-time building: memorial grove.
growing_villages.special.roots_of_the_road.deferred_policy=Future policy: lore and a one-time building, with no current item reward.

growing_villages.special.oath_of_care.title=Oath of Care
growing_villages.special.oath_of_care.summary=After an old hardship, help must become a habit rather than a stroke of luck.
growing_villages.special.oath_of_care.step_01.objective=Prepare cloth, bread, and light for future quiet wards.
growing_villages.special.oath_of_care.step_01.success=Care begins with a simple store waiting for the person who needs it.
growing_villages.special.oath_of_care.step_02.objective=Gather paper, bottles, and timber for orderly care supplies.
growing_villages.special.oath_of_care.step_02.success=Useful supplies are gathered without promises of miracles or risk to the village.
growing_villages.special.oath_of_care.step_03.objective=Prepare beds, buckets, and light for a quiet ward.
growing_villages.special.oath_of_care.step_03.success=Trust returns where help can wait in silence.
growing_villages.special.oath_of_care.completion=The oath of care is complete; a future ward will stand for mutual trust.
growing_villages.special.oath_of_care.build=Future one-time building: village infirmary.
growing_villages.special.oath_of_care.deferred_policy=Future policy: lore and a one-time building, with no current item reward.

growing_villages.special.tools_for_all.title=Tools for All
growing_villages.special.tools_for_all.summary=Craft serves the settlement when supplies and labour belong to more than one person.
growing_villages.special.tools_for_all.step_01.objective=Gather stone, coal, and timber for a civic workshop.
growing_villages.special.tools_for_all.step_01.success=The workshop has a firm footing and an honest fuel store.
growing_villages.special.tools_for_all.step_02.objective=Prepare iron, redstone, and rails as a moderate shared stock.
growing_villages.special.tools_for_all.step_02.success=Materials are ready for work that serves the village rather than private gain.
growing_villages.special.tools_for_all.step_03.objective=Gather stone bricks, iron nuggets, and light for a common store.
growing_villages.special.tools_for_all.step_03.success=The shared stock is ready: tools will be able to help many hands.
growing_villages.special.tools_for_all.completion=The civic craft arc is complete; a future workshop will be the result of shared labour.
growing_villages.special.tools_for_all.build=Future one-time building: civic workshop.
growing_villages.special.tools_for_all.deferred_policy=Future policy: lore and a one-time building, with no current item reward.

# Planned L19–20 final-city lore: contract data only; not current journal UI
growing_villages.chapter.chapter.19.founders_assembly.title=Founders' Assembly
growing_villages.chapter.chapter.19.founders_assembly.intro=Memory became a garden, care became a shared promise, and craft became public service. Now the village can gather in its own hall.
growing_villages.chapter.chapter.19.founders_assembly.requirements=Future town-hall supplies: 256 stone bricks, 128 dark oak planks, 24 bookshelves, and 16 lanterns.
growing_villages.chapter.chapter.19.founders_assembly.build_complete=The founders' hall will become the visible result of shared decisions and memory of the road.
growing_villages.chapter.chapter.19.founders_assembly.locked=The founders' assembly awaits completion of the previous path.
growing_villages.chapter.chapter.19.founders_assembly.out_of_order=This step cannot be prepared before the settlement completes the work before it.

growing_villages.chapter.chapter.20.light_of_the_village.title=Light of the Village
growing_villages.chapter.chapter.20.light_of_the_village.intro=The village has gathered in its own hall and now carries a visible light for those still following the road.
growing_villages.chapter.chapter.20.light_of_the_village.requirements=Future town-hall supplies: 320 stone bricks, 96 dark oak logs, 16 soul lanterns, and 24 glass panes.
growing_villages.chapter.chapter.20.light_of_the_village.build_complete=The village beacon will complete the path's lore without granting power or endless services.
growing_villages.chapter.chapter.20.light_of_the_village.locked=The light of the village awaits completion of the founders' assembly.
growing_villages.chapter.chapter.20.light_of_the_village.out_of_order=The final light cannot be prepared before the founders' hall is complete.

