growing_villages.sentinel.arc.signal_fire.title=The Arrow That Never Arrived
growing_villages.sentinel.arc.signal_fire.intro=For twenty winters the watchman has looked the same way, waiting for an answer.
growing_villages.sentinel.arc.signal_fire.locked=The watchman will not leave his slit until the village stands on its own feet. Come back once the mine is open.
growing_villages.sentinel.arc.signal_fire.complete=An answering fire burns beyond the ridge every night now. The village is not alone any more.
growing_villages.sentinel.arc.signal_fire.step_01.title=The Empty Slit
growing_villages.sentinel.arc.signal_fire.step_01.intro=You can see further from here than anyone would like. That winter I sent a signal arrow over the ridge, and nobody answered. I have stood here without fire and without a bow ever since. Start small: the brazier is empty, and at night I am blind.
growing_villages.sentinel.arc.signal_fire.step_01.complete=It caught. At least now I can see what I am looking at. Go to the blacksmith - he is the only one who remembers how watch arrowheads were forged.
growing_villages.sentinel.arc.signal_fire.step_02.title=Heads For The Watch
growing_villages.sentinel.arc.signal_fire.step_02.intro=The watchman sent you? So he finally decided. A signal head is not plain iron: it is tempered together with flint so it throws a spark in flight. Bring me both.
growing_villages.sentinel.arc.signal_fire.step_02.complete=Keep the first arrows, the rest go to the watch. But arrows without a target are just iron. Go to the cartographer - only he knows where the second post stood.
growing_villages.sentinel.arc.signal_fire.step_03.title=Where To Look
growing_villages.sentinel.arc.signal_fire.step_03.intro=The second post? It was on my old scraps: the ridge beyond the river, three days out. To redraw that properly I need paper and a compass - you cannot lay such a line by eye.
growing_villages.sentinel.arc.signal_fire.step_03.complete=Here is the watch line: tower, ridge, the old crossing. An arrow has to clear it, and for that it needs fletching. Ask the farmer - his coop is not standing empty.
growing_villages.sentinel.arc.signal_fire.step_04.title=Feather And Sinew
growing_villages.sentinel.arc.signal_fire.step_04.intro=Feathers? I have them. We raised that coop together, if you remember. A bowstring is not spun from air either - bring sinew. I will fletch the arrows myself; my father taught me that before he taught me to plough.
growing_villages.sentinel.arc.signal_fire.step_04.complete=The arrows are ready, take the bread for the road. What is left is why nobody answered back then, and that is not my business. Ask the miner about the old drift under the ridge.
growing_villages.sentinel.arc.signal_fire.step_05.title=What Was Closed From Within
growing_villages.sentinel.arc.signal_fire.step_05.intro=The drift under the ridge? We buried it that winter and never regretted it. But if you want a look inside, the timber and the light are on you. I go down, you wait up top.
growing_villages.sentinel.arc.signal_fire.step_05.complete=Found it. A rusted arrowhead with someone else's mark - not ours. So they did answer that winter; the arrow simply never cleared the ridge. Take it to the watchman. For twenty winters he thought he had shouted into nothing.
growing_villages.sentinel.arc.signal_fire.step_06.title=An Answer Twenty Winters Late
growing_villages.sentinel.arc.signal_fire.step_06.intro=Another post's mark. So they answered - they answered, and I did not see it. Fine. This time the arrow will carry. Give me a bow and sinew and I will build the signal one, and this village will never stand without a watch line again.
growing_villages.sentinel.arc.signal_fire.step_06.complete=The arrow goes up, flares over the forest and falls beyond the ridge. One breath, another - and an answering fire rises over the ridge. Twenty winters. Keep the bow, it is yours now: I have a tower, you have the road. And here is the map - everything I can see from up here. Unroll it wherever you want to start.
